{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/11094-game-ideas-you-ll-never-use","id":11094,"title":"Game Ideas You'll Never Use","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-15T00:13:17-08:00","id":11094,"title":"Game Ideas You'll Never Use","content":"Well, &quot;never&quot; doesn't always turn out to be true. Still, I think most of us have dreamed up a few ideas - perhaps a thematic and longrunning campaign arc, a bizarre new setting for adventures, or a character who instantly takes on a life of their own - which we have then had to keep shelved indefinitely. Usually for some stupid reason like &quot;it's my turn to run the game&quot;, or &quot;the group really doesn't feel like playing that&quot;, or &quot;you don't have a group, remember, that's why you're talking to yourself about this.&quot; :P<br /> <br /> So in the spirit of listing out my dusty ideas and rummaging magpie-like through yours: what unrealized dreams do you have for your games?<br /> <br /> (Two examples of mine to get started, nothing important lies past this point):<br /> <br /> - I'd like to run a Promethean campaign which questions whether the Pilgrimage is a good thing and leaves the answer open-ended. Maybe I'd even offer the players the choice to cheat the Pilgrimage, instead of just completing it or rejecting it.<br /> <br /> - I'd like to play a fantasy setting where humans aren't given any special central role. They're present, but are of no relative importance, and nobody pays them any special attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 11-15-2013, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T00:45:27-08:00","id":11103,"title":"","content":"My Mage Chronicle where the PCs will find here and there what appear to be Artifacts and turned out to be container of the pieces of the Arkithekton.... and an Epic Battle ensues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T02:03:58-08:00","id":11121,"title":"","content":"I've wanted, for a long time, to play a low fantasy game set in the Roman empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T04:15:00-08:00","id":11159,"title":"","content":"Most of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T06:56:03-08:00","id":11240,"title":"","content":"Using some of the elements from the Anita Blake series, such as vampires being &quot;out of the coffin&quot; and the latest sub-culture/group to become &quot;trendy&quot;. Lycanthropy being a communicable disease and being treated like AIDS. Necromancers being employed by lawyers to finalize wills or by therapists for the patients to have closure with someone who's dead.<br /> <br /> Just that kind of &quot;the supernatural doesn't hide&quot; stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:22:39-08:00","id":11299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/11094-game-ideas-you-ll-never-use?p=11121#post11121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've wanted, for a long time, to play a low fantasy game set in the Roman empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, it's my fault this last time. Sort of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T10:15:02-08:00","id":11392,"title":"","content":"I've had an idea for a WtA game for a while. The idea is that instead of the typical fight against the apocalypse until it happens they intentionally cause it, kill the wyrm and have the weaver take his place until they can return the wyrm uncorrupted to the balance. Unfortunately when I first had this idea I was in a group that if they didn't have combat going on every 20 minutes they would get bored and I didn't want the game to just be combat. And yes, I know this flies in the face of some of the metaplot. I was reminded a hundred times by the Encyclopedia guy we had in the group. You know the guy, the guy who whenever you try to do something that doesn't follow the metaplot he pipes up and says something. <br /> <br /> I have also had an idea for a Hunter game involving the Bale Hounds. Was basically just go around, investigating these strange murders. then you find out that a Bale Hound pack is helping a murder spirit and terror spirit do their thing and just terrorize a populace. I got a couple of sessions of that one under my belt and dropped it because everyone thought playing hunters meant shooting everything that moved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T12:02:05-08:00","id":11458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/11094-game-ideas-you-ll-never-use?p=11392#post11392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had an idea for a WtA game for a while. The idea is that instead of the typical fight against the apocalypse until it happens they intentionally cause it, kill the wyrm and have the weaver take his place until they can return the wyrm uncorrupted to the balance....And yes, I know this flies in the face of some of the metaplot. I was reminded a hundred times by the Encyclopedia guy we had in the group. You know the guy, the guy who whenever you try to do something that doesn't follow the metaplot he pipes up and says something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know how that works. They may go along with it, but they still want to tell you over and over that it's non-canonical and therefore doesn't really &quot;count&quot;. It's really limiting, because there's so much more fascinating stuff you can do with some subversion. Dismissing that stuff as invalid because it doesn't match up with official materials - well, it really misses the forest for the trees.<br /> <br /> I always thought it'd be cool if I could run a group of entirely new players for that reason. With no preconceptions to work against, I could make up new stuff or just play out the official material, and either way they'd find it new and exciting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T15:00:19-08:00","id":11605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/11094-game-ideas-you-ll-never-use?p=11299#post11299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, it's my fault this last time. Sort of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only sort of. I was out voted, that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T21:33:09-08:00","id":11873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/11094-game-ideas-you-ll-never-use?p=11458#post11458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always thought it'd be cool if I could run a group of entirely new players for that reason. With no preconceptions to work against, I could make up new stuff or just play out the official material, and either way they'd find it new and exciting.</div> </div> </div> </div>everytime I'm going to run a new game with my players I always try to pick a new system or setting just to subvert this problem. it drives them crazy but I'm not wanting for cool ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:41:30-08:00","id":13349,"title":"","content":"Had an idea for a character in Exalted who was motivated to create an organization that would rival the Guild. Could fight if necessary but preferred bureaucracy and would have merchants as followers. It was all about starting with nothing a building an economic empire. But I'm usually the Storyteller and not a player, so we decided to go with a rotational game-running, starting with me but I had too many games running at the time to get it going. Bet I can still get players, though.<br /> <br /> Also had an idea for an Innocents game tied in with Changeling, involving the characters being students at a boarding school run by True Fae Loyalists, but I never got the kinks ironed out so I never got it started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T12:47:59-08:00","id":13557,"title":"","content":"One character I kept wanting to play and only kind of got to (I built the character and within 3 sessions everything was taken away from him due to railroading) was Jimmy, the Nosferatu Ordo Dracul Human Farmer. He had a huge storage facility at the harbor, hundreds of thousands of square feet that provided the city with a safe haven for feeding. All of his humans were born into tthis captivity and didn't know a life other than it existed. I thought it was bizarre enough to fit well with a Nosferatu trying to discover his beast by using humans as toys and pets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:29:48-07:00","id":440941,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what system this would be for, probably one of the Mages or Changelings.<br /> <br /> You know how periodically there are those songs that kind of just catch on? &quot;Let it Go&quot;, &quot;Father and Son&quot;, even &quot;Tik Tok&quot;. The songs might not necessarily be <i>good</i>, but for some reason you can't turn around without hearing them, and people are invoking lyrics as arguments for or against certain points. That's not an accident; these stories are signals from an entity trapped too many eons ago to count, and it's taken this long to learn how to reach out even that little. The songs literally shape how people think; tiny amounts individually, but slowly slowly the entity is bringing about the conditions required to release it.<br /> <br /> Course, there's a deeper problem: people have become dependent on these stimulations. After so many centuries of being slowly engineered by these songs, peoples ability to direct themselves, previously humanities greatest power, has weakened. If they were just stopped, then so would humanity. Unfortunately, if they aren't stopped, the entity will be released, and risk the whole of reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:42:04-07:00","id":441294,"title":"","content":"Deadlands game. The heroes are on a hunt for treasure buried deep in a particularly taboo area of the Coyote Confederation. It's up to them to figure out ways to sneak past the sentries, to fight without being overheard or caught, locate the hidden treasure, and retrieve it, only to find out the gold chits were never crafted by human hands and the heroes all share in a horrible curse that can only be resolved once they've settled up with the gold's inhuman makers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T05:57:01-07:00","id":442437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/11094-game-ideas-you-ll-never-use?p=440941#post440941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what system this would be for, probably one of the Mages or Changelings.<br /> <br /> You know how periodically there are those songs that kind of just catch on? &quot;Let it Go&quot;, &quot;Father and Son&quot;, even &quot;Tik Tok&quot;. The songs might not necessarily be <i>good</i>, but for some reason you can't turn around without hearing them, and people are invoking lyrics as arguments for or against certain points. That's not an accident; these stories are signals from an entity trapped too many eons ago to count, and it's taken this long to learn how to reach out even that little. The songs literally shape how people think; tiny amounts individually, but slowly slowly the entity is bringing about the conditions required to release it.<br /> <br /> Course, there's a deeper problem: people have become dependent on these stimulations. After so many centuries of being slowly engineered by these songs, peoples ability to direct themselves, previously humanities greatest power, has weakened. If they were just stopped, then so would humanity. Unfortunately, if they aren't stopped, the entity will be released, and risk the whole of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Memethulhu. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:23:21-07:00","id":442635,"title":"","content":"Not one which I will &quot;never&quot; use, just one that will take a long, long time to fully flesh out and play, is my idea for a new Vampire template (as in, what could come after nWoD):<br /> <br /> Upon being embraced, mortals permanently lose access to their bodies. Heaven and Hell forever shut them out and the Judgement of God(s) will never find them. A powerful, quasi-spirit entity possesses the body and, unaware of its nature and origins, assumes to be the damned mortal herself. Denied judgement and eternal rest, the homeless mortal's soul is torn up in two, separate entities: the Beast and the Man: one representing her would-be redeemed soul, the other the would-be damned one. The two torment and vie for control of their former body and its actions at the hands of the Vampiric entity.<br /> <br /> Clans share a similar, otherworldly origin: something like VtM's Tremere come from somewhere like the Supernal Realms, etc. etc. The embrace is in fact a ritual carried out by the sire to draw a similar spirit from his own realm into the mortal's body. Blood Potency measures how much of the Vampiric spirit's original power has been reclaimed. The truly ancient and powerful Vampires become aware of their true nature and origins and fight a war against the other clans, a war that began far from the material but has bled through. Humanity's suffering is but a necessary casualty, its blood the fuel with which every day they repeat the ritual that bound them to our world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or something along those lines...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 03-15-2015, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:23:47-07:00","id":456027,"title":"","content":"Old world of Darkness Game: where are group of Caitiffs have started robbing local law enforcement and as the player fail at stopping them the issue escalates to the county then to the state and to the point that it become national news and the whole Vampire society descends on the town and the players who can't seem to keep their own town in check. or they do stop them somewhere and gain a stash of loot of police equipment from police radio's to squad cars. (no police are harmed in the playing of this story line)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:43:08-07:00","id":456058,"title":"","content":"For years I've wanted to play a Vampire the Masquerade game about a coterie of diablerists. I just love the mechanic, and the idea of working your way up the chain, trying to find hideouts of increasingly more powerful and cunning and secretive vampires while also dodging blood hunts and keeping an eye out for anyone who might turn auspex on you sounds like a thrilling one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:40:08-07:00","id":456137,"title":"","content":"I had a 1e Werewolf game idea set in a pack that had only one Auspice, and each one was one of the facets provided in the <i>Signs of the Moon</i> book. They all transformed one night after the other during the same moon, and Luna brought them together because the area was almost overrun with Pure. The best shot at the Urdaga restoring balance was a batch of them to appear all at once, and try to work things out from there. The justification was that there's a little bit of each Auspice in each facet, you just have to squint and turn your head to make a hybrid Rahu/Elodoth-type character work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T18:06:04-07:00","id":458526,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to run a <i>Requiem for Rome</i> game about some characters as mortals <i>before </i>they get the Embrace to put my academic credentials to good use. Then I'd like to take those characters on a wild historical ride up to the present.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'll find the perfect group of players for that, and I'm always constrained by my intense desire to actually <i>play </i>a game of VtR, which feels like it wouldn't/couldn't happen while I'm running a long term game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T18:31:54-07:00","id":458532,"title":"","content":"Probably the grand story with the Masked Children and the Player's Pen I have in the background of my WoD games. A game that requires your players to know all of the gamelines well enough to switch between them in the middle of chapters and maybe even scenes as well as weaving multiple personal player mythologies is a bit to ambitious to actually build, but man I'd love to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T05:32:50-07:00","id":458822,"title":"","content":"A sandbox style NWoD crossover game, mainly focused on werewolves, vampires, and mortals (including hunters) but with room for other creatures if there's interest in them, set in Colorado as described in Hunting Grounds: the Rockies.<br /> <br /> A comedic NWoD mortals game set in Night Vale.<br /> <br /> A small group (around 6 people) Vampire the Masquerade LARP held at a small goth bar. This one especially is never going to happen because I really want to do it at a specific goth bar in Olympia, WA(Crypta Tropa, in case anyone has heard of it) and I don't live in Washington any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}